  22:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   @verbatim
  23:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  24:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****                     ##### GPIO Peripheral features #####
  25:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  26:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]
  27:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) Each port bit of the general-purpose I/O (GPIO) ports can be individually
  28:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         configured by software in several modes:
  29:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Input mode
ARM GAS  /var/tmp//ccWDJO8V.s 			page 2


  30:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Analog mode
  31:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Output mode
  32:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Alternate function mode
  33:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) External interrupt/event lines
  34:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  35:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) During and just after reset, the alternate functions and external interrupt
  36:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         lines are not active and the I/O ports are configured in input floating mode.
  37:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  38:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) All GPIO pins have weak internal pull-up and pull-down resistors, which can be
  39:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         activated or not.
  40:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  41:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) In Output or Alternate mode, each IO can be configured on open-drain or push-pull
  42:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         type and the IO speed can be selected depending on the VDD value.
  43:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  44:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) The microcontroller IO pins are connected to onboard peripherals/modules through a
  45:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         multiplexer that allows only one peripheral alternate function (AF) connected
  46:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****        to an IO pin at a time. In this way, there can be no conflict between peripherals
  47:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****        sharing the same IO pin.
  48:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  49:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) All ports have external interrupt/event capability. To use external interrupt
  50:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         lines, the port must be configured in input mode. All available GPIO pins are
  51:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         connected to the 16 external interrupt/event lines from EXTI0 to EXTI15.
  52:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  53:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (+) The external interrupt/event controller consists of up to 39 edge detectors
  54:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (16 lines are connected to GPIO) for generating event/interrupt requests (each
  55:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         input line can be independently configured to select the type (interrupt or event)
  56:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         and the corresponding trigger event (rising or falling or both). Each line can
  57:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         also be masked independently.
  58:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  59:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****                      ##### How to use this driver #####
  60:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   ==============================================================================
  61:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****   [..]
  62:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) Enable the GPIO AHB clock using the following function: __HAL_RCC_GPIOx_CLK_ENABLE().
  63:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  64:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) Configure the GPIO pin(s) using HAL_GPIO_Init().
  65:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Configure the IO mode using "Mode" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure
  66:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Activate Pull-up, Pull-down resistor using "Pull" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef
  67:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              structure.
  68:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In case of Output or alternate function mode selection: the speed is
  69:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              configured through "Speed" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure.
  70:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In alternate mode is selection, the alternate function connected to the IO
  71:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              is configured through "Alternate" member from GPIO_InitTypeDef structure.
  72:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) Analog mode is required when a pin is to be used as ADC channel
  73:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              or DAC output.
  74:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (++) In case of external interrupt/event selection the "Mode" member from
  75:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              GPIO_InitTypeDef structure select the type (interrupt or event) and
  76:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****              the corresponding trigger event (rising or falling or both).
  77:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  78:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) In case of external interrupt/event mode selection, configure NVIC IRQ priority
  79:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         mapped to the EXTI line using HAL_NVIC_SetPriority() and enable it using
  80:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ().
  81:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  82:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) To get the level of a pin configured in input mode use HAL_GPIO_ReadPin().
  83:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  84:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) To set/reset the level of a pin configured in output mode use
  85:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         HAL_GPIO_WritePin()/HAL_GPIO_TogglePin().
  86:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
ARM GAS  /var/tmp//ccWDJO8V.s 			page 3


  87:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****    (#) To lock pin configuration until next reset use HAL_GPIO_LockPin().
  88:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  89:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) During and just after reset, the alternate functions are not
  90:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         active and the GPIO pins are configured in input floating mode (except JTAG
  91:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         pins).
  92:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  93:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) The LSE oscillator pins OSC32_IN and OSC32_OUT can be used as general purpose
  94:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         (PC14 and PC15, respectively) when the LSE oscillator is off. The LSE has
  95:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         priority over the GPIO function.
  96:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c **** 
  97:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****     (#) The HSE oscillator pins OSC_IN/OSC_OUT can be used as
  98:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         general purpose PH0 and PH1, respectively, when the HSE oscillator is off.
  99:stm/stm32l4xx/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_gpio.c ****         The HSE has priority over the GPIO function.
